If I use `enablePropertyAnimationBlending` on the manager, then a group with weight 0.5 would write half its value. But note 25 says: "enableAnimationBlending and enablePropertyAnimationBlending fill the same single slot on a manager, so the last call wins." And note 11: "A property group's weight has no effect unless enablePropertyAnimationBlending was called on the manager."

This is problematic because:
1. I'd need to call `enablePropertyAnimationBlending` which might conflict with other things on the manager
2. Note 44: "A property whose groups all have weight 1 is not mixed: the group added last wins." So if another beacon on the same manager also has weight 1, they'd conflict.
3. Note 12: "Under enablePropertyAnimationBlending, a property with any group of weight other than 1 gets the sum of value x weight over its groups" - so if two beacons animate the same lamp, their values would be summed, which is wrong.

So the custom task approach is definitely better. Each beacon has its own task and writes directly to the lamp.

